{"type":"message","id":"4a4ceb3d","parentId":"487fbb48","timestamp":"2026-05-29T01:09:59.348Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the issue. Let me trace the calculation:\n\nLine 1044: `raw_qty = (CONFIG[\"total_capital\"] * size_pct * 10) / entry_price`\n\n- total_capital = 100 USDT (from SOUL.md: 总资金 100 USDT Testnet)\n- size_pct = 0.20 (20%)\n- Leverage multiplier = 10\n\nWait, but the comment says \"加 10x 杠杆\" in the quantity calculation. So it's:\n- margin = 100 * 0.20 = 20 USDT\n- notional = 20 * 10 = 200 USDT\n- quantity = 200 / entry_price\n\nSo for:\n- DOT at $1.198: qty = 200 / 1.198 = ~167 DOT. But the actual position was 11.7 DOT!\n- SOL at $81.91: qty = 200 / 81.91 = ~2.44 SOL. But the actual position was 4.87 SOL!\n\nWait, these are both off:\n- DOT: expected ~167, got 11.7 → way too small (~7% of expected)\n- SOL: expected ~2.44, got 4.87 → about 2x too large\n\nHmm, but 4.87 SOL at $81.91 = ~$399 notional ≈ $40 margin at 10x → double the intended 20 USDT margin.\n\nAnd 11.7 DOT at $1.198 = ~$14 notional ≈ $1.4 margin at 10x → way below the 20 USDT margin.\n\nThis is strange. Let me check if the positions were opened at different times with different capital/margin settings, or if there's some bug in the quantity calculation.\n\nActually wait - the DOT was just closed at TP1. Let me focus on the current positions.\n\nLet me also check the actual quantity calculation more carefully. The format_quantity function takes symbol precision into account.\n\nLet me check what CONFIG actually has for these values.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_inhyXrJwbpF6oVxIx4B67619","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('crypto_state.json') as f:\n    state = json.load(f)\n# Show open positions details\nfor k in ['open_positions', 'positions']:\n    v = state.get(k, {})\n    if v:\n        print(f'{k}:')\n      