{"type":"message","id":"879fb24b","parentId":"1423cfd0","timestamp":"2026-05-29T01:10:37.765Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can piece together what happened:\n\n1. **DOT (11.7 QTY)**: The DOT position was originally opened at 156.9 DOT on May 25 @ $1.275. Then on May 27 it went SHORT at 158.5. Then it seems to have gone through some partial closes or position reverses. The 11.7 DOT at $1.198 entry must be a remnant from partial closes. The TL;DR: DOT was a leftover small position that wasn't the standard size. It was already closed at TP1 (09:02 today).\n\n2. **SOL (4.87 QTY)**: This is 2x the standard size. Let me check when SOL was first opened.\n\nLet me look for SOL's opening.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_UZxL3XPi1GD67f9XeUzU1178","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw && grep \"SOL.*开多\\|SOL.*开空\\|开多.*SOL\\|开空.*SOL\" logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | tail -10","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1753,"output":425,"cacheRead":65408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67586,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780017031635}}
