{"type":"message","id":"f1b4cd49","parentId":"66f04cbd","timestamp":"2026-05-29T01:10:49.662Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so SOL was originally opened at 2.38 QTY (correct per the rule). But now it's 4.87. This means either:\n1. There was a position reverse (SHORT → LONG) and the quantity changed\n2. There was an add-to-position\n3. Something else\n\nLet me check what happened around May 28-29 that changed the SOL position from 2.38 to 4.87.\n\nActually, earlier I found that on May 29 at 00:45:43 there was a SOL buy of 4.87 at $81.88 with realized PNL of -3.9342. And at 00:46:20 another SOL buy of 2.49 at $81.94 with 0 realized PNL.\n\nSo:\n- First there was a SOL SHORT at 2.38 qty @ ~$84\n- Then it was closed at a loss (probably the 4.87 buy was closing 2.38+2.49 ≈ 4.87 short, with the PNL realized at -3.93)\n- Then the system opened a new LONG at 2.49 (the second buy)\n\nWait, that doesn't add up either. 2.38 + 2.49 = 4.87. So:\n- Original SHORT: 2.38 SOL (opened at ~$84)  \n- Position was reversed (closed short + opened long) resulting in 4.87 SOL LONG position\n\nActually, let me re-read. The trade at 00:45:43 was BUY 4.87 @ 81.88 with -3.9342 realized. If this was a SHORT being closed, buying 4.87 would close a short of 4.87 SOL. But the original short was only 2.38...\n\nWait, maybe SOL went through multiple reverses:\n1. May 26: SHORT 2.38 @ $84.15 \n2. May 27: SHORT 2.38 @ $84.13 → now total short: 4.76 SOL\n3. Then there was some close/reverse that increased it further to 4.87\n\nOr maybe there's a position reversal bug where when reversing (SHORT → LONG), it buys double the quantity. Let me check the reversal logic.\n\nActually, let me re-focus. The user is asking two specific things:\n1. DOT was 14 USDT (small) — DOT was 11.7 * $1.198 = ~$14 notional. This is way below the 200 USDT standard.\n2. SOL is 400 USDT (large) — SOL is 4.87 * $82 = ~$400 notional. This is 2x the 200 USDT standard.\n\nLet me check the reversal logic to see if there's a bug that explains both.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_gd0O8FRGNs94apZHwvg43783","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw && grep \"SOL\" logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"reverse\\|反转\\|反手\\|平仓\" | tail -15","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":296,"output":1306,"cacheRead":67328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68930,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780017037932}}
