{"type":"message","id":"393560be","parentId":"e2ff6382","timestamp":"2026-05-29T09:25:03.926Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to carefully check the rotation code for potential conflicts. Let me think about this:\n\n1. The rotation code closes `weakest['symbol']` then falls through to open `sym`\n2. But `close_position` might be async or have side effects I'm not seeing\n3. I need to check if `close_position` function exists and how it works\n4. I also need to check if `save_positions` function exists\n5. The flow could have issues with `opened_this_loop` counter vs `actual_count`\n\nLet me trace through the code carefully:\n\n```python\nfor sym in CONFIG[\"symbols\"]:\n    is_full = actual_count + opened_this_loop >= CONFIG[\"max_positions\"]\n    if is_full:\n        # ... rotation logic ...\n        if weakest and new_score >= weakest_score + 20:\n            close_result = close_position(\n                weakest[\"symbol\"], weakest[\"type\"],\n                reason=f\"轮换替换（{sym}信号{new_score}分 > {weakest['symbol']}{weakest_score}分+20）\"\n            )\n            if close_result and close_result.get(\"success\"):\n                positions = [p for p in positions if p[\"symbol\"] != weakest[\"symbol\"]]\n                save_positions(positions)\n                opened_this_loop += 1\n                actual_count -= 1\n                # FALLS THROUGH to open sym position\n            else:\n                continue\n        else:\n            continue\n\n    # Falls through here after rotation success\n    ind = indicators[sym]\n    pd = prices[sym]\n    regime = detect_regime(ind)\n    fr = fr_cache.get(sym, 0)\n\n    score, direction = calc_score(\n        sym, pd, ind, regime, fg_cache, fr, btc_ind\n    )\n```\n\nWait, there's a problem! When the rotation succeeds and we fall through, we recalculate `score` and `direction` using `calc_score`. But we might get a different result from `new_score` and