{"type":"message","id":"56e8ac4a","parentId":"3321a3e1","timestamp":"2026-05-29T09:26:39.609Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now also need to handle the case where weakest is None or weakest['symbol'] == sym — in the current code, the `else` branch at 2414 logs \"轮换不达标\". But if weakest is None or symbol == sym, the fallthrough to the else branch would be misleading. Let me check.\n\nActually, looking at the code flow:\n1. `if weakest and weakest.get(\"symbol\") != sym and new_score >= weakest_score + 20:` → ROTATE\n2. `else` → log \"轮换不达标\" and continue\n\nBut if `weakest is None` (no valid positions to evaluate), or `weakest['symbol'] == sym`, the else branch logs \"轮换不达标\" which is misleading. Let me fix this.\n\nWait, if weakest is None, weakest_score would be 999 (initialized value). Then `new_score >= weakest_score + 20` would be false (since new_score is at most 100, and 100 < 1019). So it would fall to the else branch and log \"轮换不达标 (新X vs 最弱999，需≥1019)\". That's not great but not harmful.\n\nFor `weakest['symbol'] == sym`, with my fix, it also falls to else. It would log \"轮换不达标\" which is incorrect — the real reason is \"same symbol, skipping self-replacement.\"\n\nActually, let me just make the else message more specific. Or better, add a separate condition for self-replacement.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Uj5R386kqDOEYXphUHUy7673","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","new_string":"                            if weakest is None:\n                                log.info(f\"⚠️ {sym} 已达最大持仓，无有效持仓可评估轮换\")\n                                continue\n                            if weakest.get(\"symbol\") == sym:\n                                log.info(f\"⚠️ {sym} 已有持仓，跳过自替换\")\n                                continue\n                            if new_score >= weakest_score + 20:\n                          