{"type":"message","id":"8fdad5d1","parentId":"5387f76e","timestamp":"2026-05-29T09:26:57.174Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the else now correctly catches \"score not high enough\" since I already handled weakest=None and self-replacement with continue above. The else branch now correctly says \"轮换不达标\".\n\nBut wait - there's a syntax issue. My code is:\n\n```python\nif weakest is None:\n    ...\n    continue\nif weakest.get(\"symbol\") == sym:\n    ...\n    continue\nif new_score >= weakest_score + 20:\n    ...\nelse:\n    log.info(...轮换不达标...)\n    continue\n```\n\nBut if `weakest` is None, we continue. At the point of `if new_score >= weakest_score + 20`, `weakest` is guaranteed to be not None. So `weakest_score` is valid. Good.\n\nBut what if `weakest_score` is still 999 (no valid positions found)? Actually if weakest is None, we already continued. So weakest is not None here, and weakest_score is some real score. The `else` branch might still show `weakest_score=999` if all positions had invalid indicators, but that's a very edge case.\n\nActually, wait. There's a logic flow issue. When I `continue` on `weakest is None`, I skip the rest of the for loop for this symbol and go to the next symbol. That's correct.\n\nWhen I `continue` on `weakest.get(\"symbol\") == sym`, I skip too. Correct.\n\nWhen I `continue` on rotation failure (close_result not success), I skip. Correct.\n\nWhen the else branch executes (score not high enough), I `continue`. Correct.\n\nAnd when rotation succeeds, I DON'T continue — I fall through to the normal open code. Correct.\n\nLet me verify syntax now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Lb1kaIP42c6cShlu10b14875","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"import py_compile; py_compile.compile('crypto_signal_monitor.py', doraise=True); print('✅ PASS')\" 2>&1","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","pr