{"type":"message","id":"6571d604","parentId":"9d8886a4","timestamp":"2026-05-29T10:04:55.836Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two places to fix:\n\n1. Line 1199-1201: The `close_position` function's P&L calculation — uses standard position size:\n```python\npnl_usdt = CONFIG[\"total_capital\"] * CONFIG[\"position_size_pct\"] * LEVERAGE * pnl_pct * size_ratio\n```\n\n2. Line 662-666: The monitoring P&L calculation in `check_exits_fast` or similar — also might use standard size.\n\nLet me check line 662 area more carefully, and also line 1198-1206 which is the close_position function's P&L calculation.\n\nFor `close_position`: The actual qty used is `qty_raw = pos.get(\"qty\", 0) * size_ratio` which gets passed to `place_order`. The P&L should be: `qty_raw * current_price * pnl_pct` (absolute) or more precisely: `qty_raw * (current_price - entry)` for LONG and `qty_raw * (entry - current_price)` for SHORT.\n\nActually, the formula should be:\n- For LONG: `qty_raw * (current_price - entry)` — this is the notional P&L\n- For SHORT: `qty_raw * (entry - current_price)` — notional P&L\n\nWhere `qty_raw = pos.get(\"qty\", 0) * size_ratio`\n\nOR even simpler: `pos_notional * pnl_pct` where `pos_notional = qty_raw * entry`\n\nLet me look at the code around line 1198 more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_1iAUQ1WCA4jNVYLzP9Df5066","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":1196,"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","limit":12}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":619,"output":778,"cacheRead":70656,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":72053,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780049087779}}
