{"type":"message","id":"ddcd1700","parentId":"02859b35","timestamp":"2026-05-29T11:44:51.594Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API returned 4 positions at that time. So the rotation was correct — it was indeed full at 4 positions. The user saw only 3 positions because by the time they checked (19:42), SOL was already closed and only 3 remained.\n\nThe rotation correctly:\n1. Saw 4 positions on API (SOL, BNB, LINK, BTC)\n2. Evaluated LINK SHORT signal at 65\n3. Found SOL as weakest at 10\n4. Closed SOL, opened LINK SHORT\n\nAfter the rotation:\n- SOL was closed (removed)\n- Original LINK LONG was still there\n- And a new LINK SHORT should be opened\n\nWait, that's weird — having both LONG and SHORT on the same symbol? Let me check the duplicate position check in the code. After rotation closes SOL and falls through to open LINK SHORT, the code should check if LINK already has a position... \n\nLooking at the code at line 2443-2446:\n```python\napi_has_symbol = any(\n    p.get(\"symbol\") == sym and float(p.get(\"amount\", 0)) != 0\n    for p in api_positions_check\n)\nlocal_has_symbol = any(p[\"symbol\"] == sym for p in positions)\nif api_has_symbol or local_has_symbol:\n    log.info(f\"⚠️ {sym} 已有持仓（api={api_has_symbol}, local={local_has_symbol}），跳过重复开仓\")\n    continue\n```\n\nSo if LINK already had a LONG position, when the rotation code falls through and tries to open LINK SHORT, the duplicate check should catch it. Unless... the LINK LONG was already closed by then?\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. Maybe the rotation happened AND the LINK LONG was also closed by a separate mechanism (like TP hitting). Or maybe the LINK LONG was one of the 4 positions, and after SOL was closed (positions now 3), the code falls through and opens LINK SHORT, making it 4 again.\n\nBut wait — LINK already had a LONG position in the 4 positions. So when the rotation code checks `api_positions_check`, LINK LONG should show up