{"type":"message","id":"fa23fc07","parentId":"665dc22e","timestamp":"2026-05-29T11:45:31.275Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found a bug! At line 19:34:32:\n\n```\n[WARNING] ⚠️ 轮换异常：'float' object has no attribute 'get'\n```\n\nThe rotation closed SOL, and then tried to fall through to open LINK SHORT. But there was an exception: \"'float' object has no attribute 'get'\". This means the code tried to call `.get()` on a float.\n\nThe issue is: after rotation closes SOL, it falls through to the normal open code. The `close_position` function returns a float (pnl_usdt), not `close_result`. In the rotation code, I check `if close_result and close_result.get(\"success\")`.\n\nWait, but the log shows `✅ 平仓 SOL 轮换替换` — this means the `close_result.get(\"success\")` check passed. So the close was successful and the code fell through.\n\nThen the error `'float' object has no attribute 'get'` must have come from somewhere else in the normal open code path after falling through. Let me look at the open code path.\n\nActually, looking at the `close_position` function's return value:\n\n```python\nreturn pnl_usdt\n```\n\nLine 1280: `return pnl_usdt` — returns a float!\n\nBut in my rotation code, I check:\n```python\nif close_result and close_result.get(\"success\"):\n```\n\n`close_result` here is the return value of `close_position`, which is a FLOAT (the PnL), not a dict! So `close_result.get(\"success\")` would fail because floats don't have `.get()`.\n\nWait, but the log line shows the success check passed: `✅ 平仓 SOL 轮换替换（LINK信号65分 > SOL10分+20）` — this means `close_result` was truthy (non-zero float) and `.get(\"success\")` somehow didn't crash?\n\nNo wait, `.get()` on a float would crash. Let me re-read the log:\n\n```\n2026-05-29 19:34:32 [INFO] ✅ 平仓 SOL 轮换替换（LINK信号65分 > SOL10分+20） | 入场:81.9107 出场:82.0100 | PnL:0.12% (+0.48USDT) | 平100%仓 | ✅ 平仓成功\n```\n\nThis log is from the `close_position` function itself! Not from my rotation code. Let me check: `close_position` at line 1218 or thereabouts logs this. Then it returns `pnl_usdt` (a float).\n\nBack in the rotation code:\n```python\nclose_result = close_position(weakest, ...)  # returns pnl_usdt (float)\n\nif close_result and close_result.get(\"success\"):  # FLOAT! Can't call .get()!\n```\n\nSince `close_result` is a float (e.g., 0.48), `close_result` is truthy. Then `close_result.get(\"success\")` crashes with `'float' object has no attribute 'get'`.\n\nBut the log shows:\n```\n2026-05-29 19:34:32 [WARNING] ⚠️ 轮换异常：'float' object has no attribute 'get'\n```\n\nWhich means the exception catcher caught it and logged it, but also the `close_position` was already executed (SOL was closed successfully). The rotation code's exception handler catches it and continues.\n\nBut the critical issue: after the exception in rotation code, the `close_result.get(\"success\")` check was the exception point. This means:\n1. `close_result` was non-zero (truthy) since SOL had +0.48 PnL\n2. The code tried `.get(\"success\")` → crash → caught by exception handler → `continue`\n\nSo `continue` was executed, meaning the code skipped the fall-through to open LINK SHORT. But the log shows:\n```\n2026-05-29 19:34:32 [WARNING] ⚠️ 轮换异常：'float' object has no attribute 'get'\n```\n\nThis warning is from the exception handler in the rotation code. Then `continue` skips to the next symbol. LINK SHORT was NOT opened. SOL was closed.\n\nThe net result: SOL got closed but LINK SHORT was never opened. The positions went from 4 to 3. That's actually correct behavior for this bug — it resulted in a proper close without opening a duplicate position.\n\nBut the bug needs to be fixed: `close_position` returns a float (PnL), not a dict with `\"success\"` key. Let me fix the rotation code to properly check if the close was successful.\n\nLooking at the existing callers:\n```python\npnl = close_position(pos, reason, size, p)\ncircuit_breaker.record_trade(pnl)\n```\n\nAnd the `close_position` function logs its own success/failure internally. If it returns a float, it was successful. If it throws an exception, it fails.\n\nSo I should change my check from:\n```python\nif close_result and close_result.get(\"success\"):\n```\nto:\n```python\nif close_result is not None and not isinstance(close_result, str):\n```\n\nOr simpler: just check `if close_result is not None` since it returns a float on success. Or even simpler, since `close_position` already logs its own success, I should just trust it and not check the return value.\n\nActually, `close_position` returns `pnl_usdt` which is always a float (could be 0.0 or negative), so `if close_result is not None` would always be True. The real error indicator is: if `close_position` throws an exception, or returns something unexpected.\n\nLet me fix the rotation code to not check `.get(\"success\")` since it's a float:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到 bug 了 🔍\n\n`close_position` 返回的是 **float**（PnL 数值），不是 dict。我写了 `.get(\"success\")`，崩了这个：\n\n```\n⚠️ 轮换异常：'float' object has no attribute 'get'\n```\n\nSOL 被成功平掉了，但 LINK SHORT 没开成——异常被 catch 后 continue 跳过了。结果刚好保住了，没造成双方向同币种冲突。\n\n立刻修复："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_etf2XTP35vDP4yCoeaa12751","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","new_string":"                                    close_result = close_position(\n                                        weakest,\n                                        f\"轮换替换（{sym}信号{new_score}分 > {weakest['symbol']}{weakest_score}分+20）\",\n                                        1.0,\n                                        prices.get(weakest[\"symbol\"], {}).get(\"price\", 0),\n                                    )\n                                    # close_position 返回 float(PnL)，异常表明失败\n                                    if isinstance(close_result, (int, float)):\n                                        positions = [p for p in