{"type":"message","id":"2339c6b3","parentId":"2f59893b","timestamp":"2026-05-29T13:18:43.559Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is bad - the rotation is happening too frequently:\n\n1. 21:03: BNB(10分) → DOT SHORT(80分) — BNB closed\n2. 21:09: DOT(40分) → BTC SHORT(65分) — DOT closed (just opened 6 min ago!)\n3. 21:12: ETH(50分) → DOT SHORT(80分) — ETH closed, DOT reopened!\n\nThe problem is clear: the rotation threshold is too low at +20 points. As soon as a new position is opened, it gets evaluated again on the next cycle and can be immediately swapped out if a better signal appears. This creates a ping-pong effect.\n\nSpecific issues:\n1. DOT was opened at 21:03 with 80 points\n2. 6 minutes later at 21:09, DOT only has 40 points (market changed) and gets swapped out for BTC(65)\n3. 3 minutes later at 21:12, DOT is back at 80 points and swaps ETH(50)\n\nThis is a disaster. We need to add:\n1. A minimum holding time for newly opened positions (e.g., 5-10 minutes)\n2. Or a higher rotation threshold\n3. Or a cooldown for the rotated position (don't rotate out a position that was just opened)\n\nLet me add a \"minimum hold time\" — skip rotation if the position has been held for less than 5 minutes. Or better, track when a position was opened and skip it in rotation if it's too fresh.\n\nActually the simplest fix: check the position's entry timestamp and skip it if it's been less than some threshold (like 5 minutes).\n\nLet me also check what positions are now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"频繁换单是因为旋转太快了——刚开的仓位 6 分钟就被踢出去，DOT 在 9 分钟内被开关了两次：\n\n```\n21:03 BNB(10) → DOT(80)  ✅\n21:09 DOT(40) → BTC(65)  ❌ 刚开6分钟又被踢\n21:12 ETH(50) → DOT(80)  ❌ DOT又回来了\n```\n\n需要加**最小持仓时间**，刚开的仓位至少稳 10 分钟不能换。马上修："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_HRqUHgUKc7QNRZ17b7jN7886","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":2380,"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","limit":35}}],"api":"openai-completi