{"type":"message","id":"f9003f94","parentId":"b7856f8c","timestamp":"2026-05-29T16:48:26.406Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_I1B2dbZVpEA92faNX0DJ6130","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py."}],"details":{"diff":"      ...\n 2443                             # 🐛 修复：AI 说震荡 → 无条件观望；AI 反向 + 高信心 → 观望\n 2444                             if ai_dir == \"震荡\":\n 2445                                 log.info(f\"⏸️ {sym} AI判断震荡市，观望（数学={direction}，AI=震荡）\")\n 2446                                 continue\n-2447                             if conflict and ai_result.get(\"confidence\", 0) > 70:\n+2447                             if conflict and ai_result.get(\"confidence\", 0) >= 70:\n 2448                                 log.info(f\"⏸️ {sym} AI与数学信号冲突({ai_result.get('confidence')}%)，观望\")\n 2449                                 continue\n 2450 \n 2451                         # 开仓前再次检查持仓数（双重保险）\n      ...","firstChangedLine":2447},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780073306398}}
{"type":"message","id":"b7601257","parentId":"f9003f94","timestamp":"2026-05-29T16:48:46.822Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now close DOT and re-open with proper size. I'll use the close_position function approach through the existing script. Let me use the close_position method via a quick script.\n\nActually, the simplest way is to use the existing `close_position` and `open_position` scripts. But we don't have those directly - we need to use the existing tools.\n\nLet me just do it via the Binance API directly - close the DOT LONG and then open a new DOT position with the right size.\n\nDOT LONG: amount=11.7, we need to sell 11.7 to close, then buy ~165 to open a proper position.\n\nWait, I should use the existing python infrastructure in the scripts directory. Let me check if there's a manual trade script.\n\nActually, the simplest way: I'll use the close_position function from the main monitor script. But that requires importing it which might have side effects. Let me just use the raw API.\n\nOr even simpler - let me write a small script that uses the close functions from the existing codebase.\n\nHmm, actually the easiest clean way is to use the existing `close_position` logic. Let me just write a quick script that does the API calls.\n\nLet me do: close DOT position by selling 11.7 DOT at market, then open a new DOT LONG with 165 DOT.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_wlOD83iZaJ9qwPCTlfG24249","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json, hmac, hashlib, ssl, urllib.request, time\n\nwith open('auto_trade_config.json') as f:\n    cfg = json.load(f)\n\nctx = ssl.create_default_context()\nctx.check_hostname = False\nctx.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_NONE\nproxy = urllib.request.ProxyHandler({'http': 'http://127.0.0.1:7890', 'https': 'http://127.0.0.1:7890'})\nopener = urllib.request.build_opener(proxy, urllib.request.HTTPSHandler(context=ctx))\nurllib.request.install_opener(opener)\n\nbase = 'https://testnet.binancefuture.com'\napi_key = cfg['binance_api']['api_key']\nsecret = cfg['binance_api']['secret_key']\n\ndef signed(method, path, body=None):\n    ts = int(time.time() * 1000)\n    qs = f'timestamp={ts}' + (f'&{body}' if body else '')\n    sig = hmac.new(secret.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    url = f'{base}{path}?{qs}&signature={sig}'\n    r = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key}, method=method)\n    return json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(r, timeout=10).read())\n\n# Step 1: Cancel all DOT algo orders\ncos = signed('GET', '/fapi/v1/openOrders', 'symbol=DOTUSDT')\nfor o in cos:\n    signed('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/order', f'symbol=DOTUSDT&orderId={o[\\\"orderId\\\"]}')\n    print(f'已撤 DOT 挂单 {o[\\\"orderId\\\"]}')\n\n# Step 2: Close DOT LONG position\nprint('平 DOT LONG 11.7...')\nresult = signed('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', f'symbol=DOTUSDT&side=SELL&type=MARKET&quantity=11.7')\nprint(f'平仓结果: orderId={result.get(\\\"orderId\\\")} status={result.get(\\\"status\\\")}')\n\ntime.sleep(2)\n\n# Step 3: Open DOT LONG with proper size (20 USDT margin × 10x = 200 USDT notional)\nprint('获取 DOT 价格...')\nprice_data = signed('GET', '/fapi/v1/ticker/price', 'symbol=DOTUSDT')\ndot_price = float(price_data['price'])\ndot_qty = round(200 / dot_price, 1)  # DOT precision is 1 decimal\nprint(f'DOT price={dot_price}, 目标 qty={dot_qty}')\n\n# Step 4: Open\nresult = signed('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', f'symbol=DOTUSDT&side=BUY&type=MARKET&quantity={dot_qty}')\nprint(f'开仓结果: orderId={result.get(\\\"orderId\\\")} status={result.get(\\\"status\\\")}')\n\ntime.sleep(2)\n\n# Step 5: Submit TP/SL algo orders\npos = signed('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', 'symbol=DOTUSDT')\npos = [p for p in pos if float(p['positionAmt']) != 0]\nif pos:\n    p = pos[0]\n    entry = float(p['entryPrice'])\n    amt = float(p['positionAmt'])\n    tp = round(entry * 1.04, 3)  # +4%\n    sl = round(entry * 0.98, 3)  # -2%\n    tp_r = signed('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', f'symbol=DOTUSDT&side=SELL&type=TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET&stopPrice={tp}&quantity={abs(amt)}')\n    sl_r = signed('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', f'symbol=DOTUSDT&side=SELL&type=STOP_MARKET&stopPrice={sl}&quantity={abs(amt)}')\n    print(f'TP={tp} algoId={tp_r.get(\\\"orderId\\\")} | SL={sl} algoId={sl_r.get(\\\"orderId\\\")}')\n    print('DONE')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":155,"output":1587,"cacheRead":70016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":71758,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780073306410}}
