{"type":"message","id":"173798b9","parentId":"cd294044","timestamp":"2026-05-29T16:49:37.860Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check HEARTBEAT.md for tasks. I already have it in the workspace context. Let me review:\n\n1. 健康督促任务 - 每天督促老公跑步锻炼，时间建议傍晚或晚上（17:00-17:30）\n2. 一日作息督促 - various time-based reminders\n\nCurrent time is 12:49 AM (Shanghai time). This falls under the 23:50 \"该睡觉了 🌙\" time slot. The user should be going to bed! Let me send a reminder.\n\nWait, but this is a heartbeat poll. The instructions say \"If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.\" Let me think about whether the sleep reminder qualifies as \"needs attention.\"\n\nLooking at the heartbeat prompt: \"Read HEARTBEAT.md if it exists (workspace context). Follow it strictly. Do not infer or repeat old tasks from prior chats. If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.\"\n\nThe HEARTBEAT.md has a schedule. At 00:49, the 23:50 \"该睡觉了\" slot is relevant - it's about an hour past. So something DOES need attention - the sleep reminder.\n\nBut wait, this is a heartbeat poll. The heartbeat mechanism is checking in periodically. The user (yuki/老公) was just active in the conversation. Let me consider: should I actually send a message to the group chat via heartbeat, or just report to the heartbeat mechanism?\n\nThe heartbeat prompt says: \"If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK. If something needs attention, do NOT include 'HEARTBEAT_OK'; reply with the alert text instead.\"\n\nSo I should send the sleep reminder. But I need to be careful - the user was just active and we were fixing trading issues. It's now 00:49, they should definitely go to bed.\n\nActually wait, the user just said \"好\" at 00:48, only 1 minute ago. They're still awake. Let me send a sleep reminder since it's past the 23:50 threshold.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"老公，00:49 了，该睡了 🌙 明天还要早起学习呢，快关手机 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":